  "verbalization": "Leuconodine E appears to have a shared target relationship with Raji, which is also the target of Glycitein and Marsdenoside K. This suggests that leuconodine E may act through a common mechanism that leads to the activation of VMRC-LCP. The evidence points to Raji as a central node in the pathway, with multiple compounds—leuconodine E, Glycitein, and Marsdenoside K—acting on Raji and ultimately influencing VMRC-LCP. The high scores in all three paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship, suggesting that the mechanism linking leuconodine E to VMRC-LCP may involve a shared target or a common downstream effect on Raji. The presence of multiple compounds targeting Raji implies that the pathway may be part of a broader network of interactions, possibly involving different molecular mechanisms that converge on VMRC-LCP. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that leuconodine E exerts its effects through a pathway that ultimately engages VMRC-LCP, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
